  "estimatedLength": "20 minutes",
  "objectives": [
    "Determine steric number by counting lone pairs and bonding domains on a central atom.",
    "Identify the five basic electron-domain geometries: linear, trigonal planar, tetrahedral, trigonal bipyramidal, and octahedral.",
    "Distinguish between electron-domain geometry and actual molecular geometry.",
    "Explain how lone pairs compress bond angles below ideal values due to heightened repulsion.",
    "Apply VSEPR predictions to specific real-world molecules including methane, ammonia, water, PF5, SF6, and XeF4."
  ],
