          "changeMeaning": "Display Methane on the left as a baseline tetrahedral molecule with no lone pairs.",
          "narration": "VSEPR theory also explains why real molecular shapes deviate from ideal angles. Let's compare three molecules that all share a steric number of 4. First, methane has four bonding pairs and zero lone pairs. Its molecular geometry is a perfect tetrahedral shape, and all bond angles are exactly 109.5 degrees."
        },
