                  "timeRate": 1.0,
                  "rotationTime": 15
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "changeMeaning": "Enable water on the right to show the cumulative effect of two lone pairs compressing the bond angle down to 104.5 degrees.",
          "narration": "Now examine water on the right. With two lone pairs, the mutual repulsion between the two non-bonding clouds, as well as their repulsion of the O-H bonds, is even stronger. This double repulsion forces the remaining hydrogen atoms closer together, compressing the bond angle down to 104.5 degrees, leaving a molecular shape that is bent."
        },
